-- Practice data for SEAITT Legazpi LMS: fills the tables so every page has something to show.
--
-- The people are the sample accounts of seaittlms_sample_accounts.sql (run that file first). This file then adds, for those people:
--   * the enrollment of the 40 students in 10 sections of the eight strands (grade 11 and grade 12, ACAD and TECH-PRO) and their courses, with the days and hours each course meets;
--   * the courses of the 12 teachers, and for each course: modules (posted, one scheduled), activities, a quiz with questions and a task performance;
--   * who opened what, the work handed in, the scores, the attendance of the last weeks (a few students are failing, so the guidance counselor has referrals);
--   * announcements, messages, notifications, friends, three groups with posts, files in the lockers, the security log, the system settings;
--   * the library of the academic provider (syllabus, modules, quizzes, sent to the teachers as drafts) and one teacher evaluation with its answers.
-- Dates are relative to the day you run it (the work is due before and after today). Names, scores and answers are made up.
--
-- How to run it: open this file in MySQL Workbench (File > Open SQL Script...), then press the lightning bolt (Execute). It can take a minute.
-- Run it ONCE, on a database where the sample students are not enrolled yet: if any of them is enrolled (or an account is missing) nothing is added,
-- and the last result says so. To start again, run seaittlms_reset_and_rebuild.sql and seaittlms_sample_accounts.sql first.

